    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0213" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v2/pg843"/>

                <head>No. 372.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General <persName corresp="#p_DES1"
                            type="from">Sickles</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received 8.49 p.m.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 3,
                        1873</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Interview with minister of state to-day. Under date of 28th ultimo, minister of
                    ultramar sent royal orders by post to captain-general of Cuba to hasten and
                    facilitate action in cases of Mora and Mueses. Telegrams likewise sent in same
                    sense respecting these and other cases of embargo. For reasons you will
                    appreciate, having reference to the situation in Cuba, this government can
                    enforce judgments of the mixed commission in favor of claimants with less
                    difficulty and delay than are incident to voluntary release.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_DES1">SICKLES</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
